# Illogical Impulse ISO — curated wallpaper pack manifest (#26 / PROPOSAL §9).
#
# FETCH-ONLY: only this few-KB TEXT manifest rides in the squashfs (Pillar 7 /
# §18 ISO-size gate). The images themselves are NEVER baked — `iictl wallpaper
# pack` downloads each into ~/Pictures/Wallpapers/showcase/ (where upstream's own
# switchwall.sh chooser looks: it `cd`s into $PICTURES/Wallpapers/showcase on a
# bare chooser run), verifies the sha256, and records the fetched set in the
# ledger so `iictl wallpaper --revert` / `iictl revert-all` delete exactly what
# was fetched — leaving the one baked default (70-assets.sh) untouched.
#
# Format, one entry per line, WHITESPACE-separated (tabs or spaces):
#
#     <filename>  <url>  <sha256>  [rev]
#
#   filename  destination basename under ~/Pictures/Wallpapers/showcase/. Must
#             contain no spaces. The `ii-` prefix marks it as a distro-fetched
#             file for a clean revert; the extension sets the image type.
#   url       direct download URL. Pinned to an immutable commit SHA so the bytes
#             (and thus the sha256) are reproducible forever.
#   sha256    lowercase 64-hex digest of the file. `iictl wallpaper pack` skips
#             any download whose digest does not match (a clear, non-fatal error).
#             validate.sh (theming coherence) fails the build if any entry lacks
#             a 64-hex sha256 — an unverifiable fetch is a bug-class.
#   rev       OPTIONAL 4th column: the source commit/tag the URL is pinned to
#             (informational — the sha256 is the real integrity gate).
#
# Curated set: seven landscape / abstract wallpapers from JaKooLit/Wallpaper-Bank,
# pinned to commit c5e1780c29adca428dc4ca2d970bd1a6a09f18f3.

